# Environment variables read by the bundled MCP server.
# Copy to .env and fill in the keys for the models you plan to use.
# The .env file is gitignored.

# --- OpenAI (GPT) ---
# Required by the official codex policy: the judgment worker dispatches
# through the openai adapter and bills this key server-side, independent of
# the codex CLI's own driver-side login (ChatGPT seat or its own API key).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# No ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. This harness never requests or uses one — the
# carried Anthropic adapters and the policies that reference them are
# non-selectable replay fixtures, not part of the official model cast.

# --- Google (Gemini) ---
# Required by any policy that routes mechanical phases to Gemini, including
# the official codex policy (Gemini 3.7 Flash mechanical tier).
#
# There are two ways to reach Gemini. Pick one; the server detects which.
#
# 1. Vertex AI — Google Cloud. No key. Run:
#
#      gcloud auth application-default login
#
#    and the server signs requests with those credentials. Calls bill the
#    Google Cloud project, so nothing below is needed unless the account has
#    more than one project, or a service account is used instead of a login.
#
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=my-project          # else read from the credentials file
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=global             # else global. Regional endpoints bill
#                                          # +10% on Gemini 3+; the reported cost
#                                          # follows, so only set this for quota.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json
#
# 2. AI Studio — an API key, for anyone without a Google Cloud project.
#    Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
# With both present the API key wins, because setting one is a deliberate
# local choice while Google Cloud credentials are often just ambient machine
# state. Set GEMINI_BACKEND=vertex or GEMINI_BACKEND=api-key to force a door.
# GEMINI_BACKEND=vertex
